## Implementation summary

### Active request registry

`llama_worker/cancellation/activeRequestRegistry.mjs` exports:

```text
createActiveRequestRegistry({ state, receiveMessageOnPort, createPromptAbortError })
```

The returned registry facade provides:

```text
createActiveRequestRecord({ id, sessionId, cancelPort })
getActiveRequest(id)
isActiveRequestAborting(record)
readCancelPortMessage(record)
synchronizeExternalCancellation(record, message)
isPromptAbortError(record, err)
buildRequestObsoleteError(requestId)
isRequestObsolete(requestId)
abortActiveRequest(record, reason)
abortActiveRequestById(id, reason)
getActiveRequestRecords(filterFn)
abortActiveRequests(filterFn, reasonFactory)
```

Behavior preserved:

- cancel ports are still unrefed during record creation;
- request sequence increments still occur at record creation;
- cancel-port polling still drains all pending packets and uses the latest cancel packet;
- non-cancel packets are ignored;
- cancellation still maps to `createPromptAbortError(...)` with existing request/session metadata;
- `AbortError` is still treated as prompt abort only while the record is aborting;
- `abortActiveRequest(...)` still marks records as `aborting` and aborts prompt/context controllers;
- abort helpers do not delete records from `state.activeRequests`;
- abort helpers do not close cancel ports.

### Request boundaries

`llama_worker/cancellation/requestBoundaries.mjs` exports:

```text
createRequestBoundaries({ requests })
```

The returned boundary facade provides:

```text
waitForActiveRequestBoundaries(records)
waitForPriorSessionRequestBoundaries(sessionId, currentRequestId)
hasActiveRequestForSession(sessionId)
```

Behavior preserved:

- waits use `Promise.allSettled(...)`, not `Promise.all(...)`;
- empty boundary waits still return `[]`;
- same-session boundary waits compare active request sequence numbers;
- current request id is excluded;
- only prior same-session records are waited;
- boundary helpers do not mutate request state.

### Worker root wiring

`llama_worker/llama.mjs` now imports and wires the two cancellation factories:

```js
import { createActiveRequestRegistry } from "./cancellation/activeRequestRegistry.mjs";
import { createRequestBoundaries } from "./cancellation/requestBoundaries.mjs";
```

`llama_worker/llama.mjs` remains the only composition root. The cancellation modules do not import `llama_worker/llama.mjs`, `workerBridge.mjs`, or parent runtime modules.

## Important invariants preserved

### Active request deletion timing

Deletion of active request records still occurs in `handlePromptMessage()` final cleanup:

```js
record.state = "done";
workerState.activeRequests.delete(id);
record.cancelPort?.close();
```

This branch intentionally does not move deletion or cancel-port closure into abort helpers.

### Same-session boundary ordering

Same-session prompt ordering still waits for prior same-session request boundaries before prompt/session work continues.

### Reset/shutdown disposal distinction

The prior model disposal policy invariant remains unchanged:

```text
resetModel      -> disposeModelStack({ operation: "reset_model" })
shutdownWorker  -> disposeModelStack({ operation: "shutdown" })
```

## Propagation review

- `tests/helpers/runtimeFixtureFiles.mjs` now includes the two new worker cancellation modules.
- Direct smoke-test `RUNTIME_FILES` arrays now include the two new worker cancellation modules.
- `workerBridge.mjs` still targets `./llama_worker/llama.mjs`.
- No module under `llama_worker/**` imports `llama_worker/llama.mjs` or `workerBridge.mjs`.
- No parent runtime file was changed.
- No worker protocol message shape was changed.

