## Caveats / known risks

```text
Finding:
This branch moves cancellation helpers out of the worker root but still leaves prompt, context/session, lifecycle, and router logic inline.
Affected surface:
llama_worker/llama.mjs request cancellation, boundary waits, and prompt final cleanup.
Why it matters:
Early request deletion or cancel-port closure would break same-session boundary waits and reset/shutdown cleanup ordering.
Smallest safe correction:
Keep active request deletion and cancel-port close in handlePromptMessage() final cleanup only.
What still needs verification:
Michael real-runtime cancellation/context-boundary gates before merge-readiness language.
```

```text
Finding:
Sandbox/mock tests passed, but they do not prove native/model behavior.
Affected surface:
worker cancellation, context creation cancellation, prompt streaming, reset/shutdown boundary timing.
Why it matters:
This branch touches cancellation surfaces that interact with real node-llama-cpp/native behavior.
Smallest safe correction:
Run the recommended real-runtime carry-forward gates locally before treating the branch as merge-ready.
What still needs verification:
real-runtime-tested by Michael.
```

## Recommended real-runtime gates

```bash
SMOKE_MODE=real-fresh-session-cancel-context-boundary node ./tests/smokeTestContextCreationCancelBoundary.mjs
SMOKE_MODE=real-cancel-new-session-followup-shutdown node ./tests/smokeTestRealRuntimeContextCancelShutdownDiagnostics.mjs
SMOKE_MODE=real-cancel-same-session-followup-shutdown node ./tests/smokeTestRealRuntimeContextCancelShutdownDiagnostics.mjs
SMOKE_MODE=real-cancel-same-session-followup-reset-new-session-then-shutdown node ./tests/smokeTestRealRuntimeContextCancelShutdownDiagnostics.mjs
